{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_009: multimodal, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, singleprofile, concat fusion, acc≈0.53), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually adding value over a single-modality baseline. config_002 (image_only, singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l) is the cleanest controlled comparison: it removes the RNA modality while keeping the identical image encoder, profile setting, and overall architecture, isolating the contribution of RNA and the fusion mechanism. If image-only approaches or exceeds 0.53, the multimodal premise is questionable and budget should shift toward single-modality optimization; if it is substantially lower, it validates the multimodal direction and justifies further investment in fusion/aggregation/profile design. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the foundational design decision (is multimodal worth the complexity?) before committing budget to finer-grained comparisons like encoder choice, aggregation, or multiprofile settings."
}

